{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-158743","model_call":55,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q44"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q44"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_143315727#9_386186229","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q44","rank":2,"snippet":"revolution of 1848 really two revolutions? What two European countries were not affected by the Revolution of 1848? The 1789 French Revolution is called the Springtime of Peoples? What happened as a result of Russian revolution? How did the development of Russia cause a revolution? The Revolution influenced a series of revolts that came to be known as the Springtime of Peoples? \" , \"segment\": \"Many countries were involved in the European revolutions of 1848 such as France, Italy, <cover>Germany, the Netherlands, Poland, and Austria. However, this uprising had little political impact though it eliminated feudalism in Austria and Prussia and inspired reform in Denmark and the Netherlands. Was the revolution of 1848 </cover>successful? i woudnt say yes, i wouldnt say no. How was the French revolution of 1848 really two revolutions? by asuckinasdnf dsfdsfsfadsgfvasfgdf What two European countries were not affected by the Revolution of 1848? Great Britain and Russia The 1789 French Revolution is called the Springtime of Peoples? The answer is FALSE, it was the revolutions of 1848. What happened as a result of Russian revolution? As a result of the Russian Revolution, Communists gained control of Russia.\" , \"start_char","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_143315727#9_386186229","rank":2,"relevance":1}]},"time":6},"model_calls":55,"document_judgments":26,"relevance_3":9,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
