{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-158743","model_call":57,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1848 revolutions\" \"germany\" \"netherlands\" (+ reforms uprisings monarchy))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"1848 revolutions\" \"germany\" \"netherlands\" (+ reforms uprisings monarchy))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1560430529#1_3281721615","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q46","rank":1,"snippet":"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1560430529#1_3281721615\" , \"end_char\": 3053.000000 , \"headings\": \"Revolutions of <cover>1848 Revolutions of 1848 European history History at your fingertips \" , \"segment\": \"In Belgium, the Netherlands, and Denmark it manifested itself in peaceful reforms of existing institutions, but democratic insurrections broke out in the capitals of the three great monarchies, Paris, Vienna, and Berlin, where the governments, rendered powerless by their fear of “the revolution,” did little to defend themselves. The revolution was successful in France alone; the Second Republic and universal manhood suffrage were established, but the quarrel between the supporters of the république démocratique and the partisans of république démocratique et sociale culminated in a workers’ insurrection in June 1848. In Austria, where the new ministers promised to grant constitutions, the monarchy withstood the storm, and in Prussia King Frederick William IV, who led the movement for the unification of Germany, </cover>hoisted the black, red, and gold flag that had become the symbol of German unity. The German governments agreed to the convocation of three constituent assemblies at Berlin, Vienna, and Frankfurt ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1560430529#1_3281721615","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":57},"model_calls":57,"document_judgments":27,"relevance_3":9,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
